34. Termination
Your rights under this License terminate automatically if you materially violate its conditions.
A material violation includes, without limitation:
creating a Modified Work under the permission granted by this License while intentionally withholding its Corresponding Source from the public;
falsely claiming that a Modified Work is exempt from the universal source-publication requirement;
Conveying a Covered Work without the required License and source notices;
Conveying a Covered Work without the required Upstream Repository disclosure;
commercially offering a Covered Work without the required point-of-sale disclosures;
imposing additional restrictions prohibited by this License; or
otherwise materially violating the conditions of this License.
If you cease all violation of this License, your permissions are automatically reinstated:
provisionally, unless and until the Copyright Holder explicitly and finally terminates your rights; or
permanently, if the Copyright Holder does not notify you of the violation within a reasonable period after your cessation.
Rights previously granted to downstream recipients who remain compliant with this License are not automatically terminated merely because another recipient violates this License.
A Copyright Holder may permanently terminate your rights only after you have been given a reasonable opportunity to correct the violation, except where applicable law permits otherwise.
Termination does not invalidate rights independently acquired by other recipients who received the Covered Work lawfully and remain compliant with this License.
35. Acceptance
You are not required to accept this License merely to receive or execute an unmodified copy of the Program.
However, no permission is granted to exercise copyright-controlled rights in the Covered Work except under this License or another permission separately granted by the applicable Copyright Holder.
In particular, the modification permission granted by this License is conditional upon compliance with the universal source-publication requirements of this License.
By exercising rights granted by this License, you accept its applicable conditions.
Nothing in this License is intended to restrict rights that applicable law makes impossible for a copyright holder to restrict.
